<title>PORTUGAL: Yield falls on Portugal 10-yr bonds.</title>
<headline>Yield falls on Portugal 10-yr bonds.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1997-06-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following is the result of the Portuguese Institute for Public Credit Management auction of 25 billion escudos of 10-year fixed-rate bonds (OT).</p>
<p>    ISSUER: Republic of Portugal   MATURITY: 23 Feb 2007</p>
<p>    AMOUNT PLACED: 19.91 bln esc	 COUPON: 6.625 pct</p>
<p>AVERAGE ACCEPTED YIELD: 6.559362</p>
<p>HIGHEST ACCEPTED: 6.58  LOWEST: 6.50</p>
<p>BIDS: 53.63 bln esc PAYMENT FREQUENCY: Annual</p>
<p>NOTES: The issue is fungible. The auction takes to 134.51 billion escudos the total amount of the bonds issued.</p>
</text>
